    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32337" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκλεκτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>capable of exercising moral choice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				3.46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἀξία</span> value <i>deserving such
				choice,</i> Antip.ib.<i><span class="en">
				30
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>picking out, selective,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάμεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			 fin.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐ.</span><i>the
				Eclectics,</i> philosophers <i>who selected such doctrines as
				pleased them</i> in every school, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.684
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. αἵρεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.353
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					p.41A.
				</span></i>
			</div>
